      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, coming back to this again.\n\n\u003e In the computeInitialDelay method we perform the modulo operation so the delay will always be (-interval, interval), however if delay is \u003c\u003d 0, we add interval to it so if jitter is present, delay will always be (jitter, interval + jitter].\n\nBut in this case start time is 11:30, now is 10:00, so we have 1.5 hours from now until start. Doing `Duration.between(now, startTime).toMillis() % interval` works out as \"1.5 hours % 1 hr \u003d 0.5 hr\". So actually `isAtLeast(ms(30, MINUTES))` seems correct (like L45 has).\n\nMy general point is that the jitter doesn\u0027t matter for the lower threshold because the random jitter value could be 0.",
